  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "The query molecule (warfarin) is predicted to have high oral bioavailability (F >= 20%). The strongest evidence comes from structurally analogous acidic aryl-ketone drugs ketoprofen and suprofen, both showing absolute oral bioavailability above 90% in humans. Additional high-transfer analogues with direct absolute bioavailability measurements also exceed the threshold. No affirmative evidence supports F < 20%.",
